; sound system — a dub desk: a send you throw by hand, a record that skips, a chip echo that screams
; T1 (button1) throws the rimshot into the echo; fader1 the echo's feedback (past 0.8 it runs away)
; fader2 the tone; T2 (button2) makes the record skip

2026-11-24
----------
the clk is clock 4
the rim is string 9 damp=0.6 bright=0.8
the bass is string 1 damp=0.2
the echo is dub time=0.375 tone=0.4
the skip is stutter length=0.25 decay=0.8 shrink=0.1 drop=-1

clk.half -> rim.pluck
clk.bar -> bass.pluck
rim -> echo
button1 -> echo.throw
fader1 -> echo.feedback
fader2 -> echo.tone
echo bass -> skip
button2 -> skip.trig
skip -> out

The chip
--------
; the Chloe's little black chip: fader1 its time (turn it and the pitch bends), fader2 its feedback
the clk is clock 4
the rim is string 9 damp=0.6 bright=0.8
the chip is pt2399
clk.eighth -> rim.pluck
rim -> chip
fader1 -> chip.time
fader2 -> chip.feedback
rim -> out
chip -> out

Beauty
------
; eight mirrors: a pluck fanned across the room, each reflection drifting on its own
the clk is clock 3
the note is string 6
the hall is beauty time=0.7 spread=1 feedback=0.4 jitter=0.5
the turn is reverse size=0.6 mix=1 feedback=0.3
clk.beat -> note.pluck
note -> hall
fader1 -> hall.jitter
fader2 -> hall.spread
hall.left -> left
hall.right -> right
note -> turn
turn -40> out
